@talks work:comms
// TW1, the Talk a while work pools: Comms (plans/work-pools-plan.html, decided 2026-10-20). Ids work.comms.<slug>;
// topic always "work". Messages home, the relay, the ship's channels, languages. Discreet: never what's in anyone's
// messages. Ferreira (Comms Chief) learns Veyli; Takahashi on nights. Stuck (Santos), burnout (Tran), notgood
// (Quaye): no doubt or leaving talk.

== static
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Some nights the relay's all static. You tune and tune and then, there. A voice.
them: Like picking a lock with your ears. Best feeling in Comms.   #warm
ask: What's the most satisfying fiddly thing you do?
listen: Whose voice was it?
  them: Somebody's gran, calling to say happy birthday. Twelve hours late. Still lovely.   #warm
share: Getting a stuck bolt free.
  them: Same feeling. Fiddle, fiddle, then it gives. Very good.
cheer: Opening a biscuit packet neatly.
  them: Impossible. Nobody's ever done it. You're a legend if you have.   #funny

== sorting
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:ferreira
them: Every message home passes through Comms. Sorted, sent, queued after storms.
them: We never read them. We read the envelopes. Envelopes are lovely, actually.   #warm
ask: Who do you write to most, back home?
listen: What makes an envelope lovely?
  them: People draw on them. Little stars, little ships. Kids especially. Makes my day.   #warm
share: My family. Not often enough.
  them: Write one tonight. I'll send it with the morning bag. Quickest way home.   #warm
cheer: Nobody. They write to me. Badly.
  them: Bad letters are the best letters. Keep every one.   #funny

== voices
when: tier>=acquaintance !who:farouk-olu
them: Farouk knows every voice on the ship's channels. One word and he'll name you.
them: I'm trying to learn it. I'm at about thirty voices. You're one of them now.   #warm
ask: What's a voice from home you'd know anywhere?
listen: How does he do it?
  them: He listens to how people breathe before they talk. He says it's like a signature.
share: My mum's. Even through static.
  them: That's the one everyone says. The relay can't hide a mum.   #warm
cheer: Pell's. He's very loud.
  them: Ha. Pell needs no channel. Pell is a channel.   #funny

== languages
when: tier>=colleague !who:ferreira|rossi-femi|takahashi-wen
them: Ferreira speaks four languages, and now Veyli. She practises on the Envoy. Gets corrected.
them: She says Veyli has many words for quiet. She's learnt three. She's very proud.   #warm
ask: Is there a language you'd love to speak?
listen: What are the three words for quiet?
  them: She won't say them out loud. Says they're too quiet to repeat. Very Veyli.   #funny
share: My family's old language. I only know bits.
  them: Learn a few more bits. Send them home. They'll be thrilled.   #warm
cheer: Engine. Fluently.
  them: You're halfway there. You talk to machines already. We've all seen it.   #funny

== night-comms
when: tier>=colleague who:takahashi-wen
them: Nights, the channels go quiet and I sing. Badly. Every song in the record cabinet.
them: The relay doesn't mind. It's heard worse. It's heard Torres.   #funny
ask: What do you do, when you're alone at work?
listen: Do you know all the words?
  them: Every one. Four other people say the same. We disagree on all of them.   #funny
share: Talk to the machine I'm fixing.
  them: Ha. Then we're both talking to something that won't answer. Good company.   #funny
cheer: Eat the snacks I said I'd save.
  them: Classic night shift crime. I'll never tell.   #funny

== discreet
when: tier>=colleague !who:santos-zofia|tran-chloe
them: Comms is mostly keeping quiet. Everything passes through us. Nothing passes out of us.
them: People trust you with their news before anyone else knows it. That's a lot to hold.   #warm
ask: What's something people trust you with?
listen: Is it hard, keeping it in?
  them: Sometimes. Good news is hardest. I want to cheer and I can't. I cheer later. Quietly.   #funny
share: Their machines. Fixing them right.
  them: That's big trust too. Every warm room aboard is somebody trusting you.   #warm
cheer: The last biscuit. I always save it.
  them: A sacred trust. I'm not sure I believe you.   #funny

== comms-means
when: tier>=friend
them: Know what Comms means to me? A call home at three in the morning that gets through.
them: Somebody's dad says goodnight across all that dark. I put that call through. Me.   #warm
ask: What part of your work do you hope people remember?
listen: Does it ever not get through?
  them: Sometimes. Then we try again. And again. Until it does. That's the job.   #warm
share: The things that just worked.
  them: That's the best memory to leave. "It just worked." Nobody knows it was you. Lovely.   #warm
cheer: That I was nice at the tea corner.
  them: Underrated legacy. Very Wren.   #funny

== comms-habit
when: tier>=friend
them: The job gave me a habit. I hear static in everything. The washer. The lift. Rain on leave.
them: I keep wanting to tune it. My family thinks I'm humming. I'm tuning.   #funny
ask: Has your work changed how you hear things?
listen: What's the clearest sound aboard?
  them: The mess at breakfast. Seventy people and no static at all. Just people.   #warm
share: I hear every machine's mood now.
  them: Then we're both tuning things. Just different channels.
cheer: I hear "dinner's ready" from Deck 6.
  them: That's not Comms. That's love. Of dinner.   #funny
